[{:seon.task/name "a-point-is-found-without-walking-the-branch"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.ctx.wire/at-t` finds branch db's commit holding t by walking the line back from db, a ``datahike.api/commit-as-db`` a commit, on every call; `seon.root/back-point` calls it and keeps the commit when `(= t (:max-tx at))`. Measured 2026-11-11 (LMDB, Seon's layout, one-datom commits, the point at the first of n): 379k, 4.17M and 42.1M engine ticks, 1.7, 18 and 186 MB, at n = 10, 100 and 1,000 (42k ticks and 185 KB a commit). What replaces it: ``datahike.versioning/commit-at-tx`` (Datahike pin `f47067b5`, docs/storage.md#a-points-commit): `(datahike.versioning/commit-at-tx db t)` answers `{:branch :commit :t}`, the commit of db's lineage whose last transaction t' is the greatest <= t, exact when `(= t (:t p))`; `(datahike.versioning/commit-holding-tx db t)` the commit whose span holds t, which is what at-t answers now (its earliest commit holding t). Both read each commit once per process and keep it in memory, then confirm the answer with one ``konserve.core/exists?`` (9.0k ticks): measured over the same span, a first lookup 169k, 1.69M and 16.9M ticks (one commit-record read, 16.8k ticks and 64 KB, a commit walked, plus the exists?), a repeat 9.4k (the exists? alone), k reads and the exists? after k new commits. What bounds the first walk: it stops at the first commit whose last transaction is <= t, so a resume from a recent point reads few commits and one from an old point many (a 1,000-commit-old point: 1,000 record reads). The commit graph record would read cheaper (12.6k ticks, 40 KB) but holds no max-tx; carrying the walk on it would store a derivable value, not done (owner, 2026-11-11), the number recorded for him. Change: back-point takes `(datahike.versioning/commit-at-tx db t)` and keeps `:commit` when `(= t (:t p))`, else refuses as now; at-t becomes `(d/commit-as-db (:store db) (:commit (datahike.versioning/commit-holding-tx db t)))`, and where a sweep took the commit the refusal `{:type :commit-expired :branch :tx}` (ex-info at its named edge) gives `(d/as-of db t)` as now; `:tx-after-head` and `:tx-before-first-commit` are a caller's error, never a nearby commit. Delete the walk loop."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ctx.wire-test/a-point-reads-each-commit-once}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-task-is-shown-once"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: an agent's task (its plan, proofs, cites) is in `@ctx` and drawn again whole on the model's page, so the first request holds it twice. Plan: the task whole is in `@ctx`; the model's page shows one line naming it and what is derived from it (its proofs' states, what its cites resolve to), never the plan's text again (docs/ctx.md#what-the-model-reads-and-what-the-page-renders). Deletes: the page's copy of the plan. Proof, red first: in a seeded agent's first request the plan's text appears once; a recorded request moves by exactly that part."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ctx.wire-test/the-plan-is-in-the-first-request-once}}
]
